# Coding Rules

## CSS

- Use CSS custom properties for colors, spacing, and typography
- Use `clamp(min, preferred, max)` for responsive typography on headings
- Use `aspect-ratio` to maintain image placeholder dimensions
- Organize styles by section with clear comment headers
- Mobile-first: base styles for mobile, media queries for larger screens
- Use utility classes for common patterns: `.container`, `.text-center`, `.section-padding`
- Follow BEM-like naming: `nav__list`, `service-card__title`
- Global `box-sizing: border-box;` is set - rely on it for consistent sizing

## JavaScript

- Wrap all code in `DOMContentLoaded` event listener
- Use `IntersectionObserver` for scroll-triggered animations
- Keep dependencies minimal - vanilla JS preferred
- Handle mobile navigation with: toggle states, escape key close, overlay, body scroll lock
- Booking portal uses `.hidden` class and `data-step` attributes for multi-step state management

## Accessibility

- Add ARIA attributes for interactive elements (accordion, navigation)
- Use `aria-expanded` for expandable content
- Include `aria-label` on icon-only buttons and links
- Use `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` to disable animations for users who prefer reduced motion

## Content & Tone

- Write copy in first-person, authentic practitioner voice
- Keep headlines evocative and meaningful, not just functional
- Prioritize readability: larger font sizes, good line heights

## Images

- Display full images rather than cropping when possible
- Use `object-fit: contain` or adjust `aspect-ratio` to show complete images
- Always provide alt text
- Ensure image `src` paths correctly point to the `images/` directory
- If images show 404 errors, check server logs and verify files exist locally
- When an image is missing, confirm with user whether to add it or remove the reference

## Animations

- Keep animations subtle: fades and gentle scales
- Aim for tranquil, calming effects
- Use CSS transitions or `IntersectionObserver` for scroll effects

## Placeholders

- Mark placeholder content clearly: `[Practitioner Photo]`, `[Phone Number]`
- Booking system has payment placeholder - integration not required for demo

## Workflow

- Test responsive design thoroughly across device sizes
- Verify mobile navigation works: toggle, escape, overlay click, scroll lock
- For rebranding/style changes: only change colors and brand name; preserve all functionality, animations, and layout
- Batch file updates efficiently - avoid updating the same file multiple times
- When extracting colors from external sites, ask for explicit hex values rather than trying to parse from URLs

## Dev Server

- Use `python3 -m http.server` (not `python` which may not exist)
- If port 8000 is in use, try alternate ports: `python3 -m http.server 8080`
- Check server logs for 404 errors when debugging missing assets

## Deployment

- Changes must be committed and pushed to Git to appear on deployed URLs (e.g., Vercel)
- If merging is blocked by worktree conflicts, create a Pull Request as an alternative
- After adding images locally, inform user of both the local path and localhost URL
